{#-
  Per-tenant VRF context for NX-OS symmetric IRB.

  One `vrf context` per L3 VNI. This is what makes routing BETWEEN subnets work
  across VTEPs: the L2 VNIs carry bridged traffic within a subnet, the L3 VNI is
  the tenant's transit VNI that routed traffic rides. Without it a leaf bridges
  fine and routes nothing, which presents as an EVPN failure and is not one.

  Two route-targets are deliberately emitted per VRF and they are not redundant:
  `route-target both X` applies to the VPNv4 address-family and `route-target
  both X evpn` to L2VPN EVPN. NX-OS keeps them separate and EVPN imports only
  honour the `evpn`-qualified one.

  import_route_targets are the other sites' VRF route-targets, set when a
  segment in this VRF is stretched across EVPN Multi-Site
  (transforms/helpers/vxlan.py): each fabric exports its VRF under its own
  evpn_rt_as, so without them the type-5 routes of the remote site never land.

  vrf_routes (transforms/helpers/firewall.py get_exchange_routes) are the
  statics of the inter-VRF exchange through a firewall context; they sit inside
  the VRF, not as a global `ip route ... vrf X`.

  Included by the leaf/border-leaf NX-OS templates from inside their
  `{% if vxlan and vxlan.enabled %}` guard, so `vxlan` is known non-empty here.
-#}
{%- if vxlan.l3_vni_mappings %}
!
! VRF Contexts (symmetric IRB — one L3 VNI per tenant)
!
{%- for mapping in vxlan.l3_vni_mappings %}
vrf context {{ mapping.vrf_name }}
  vni {{ mapping.l3_vni }}
{%- if vxlan.evpn.rd_format %}
  rd {{ vxlan.evpn.rd_format | replace('{vni}', mapping.l3_vni | string) }}
{%- endif %}
{%- for route in vrf_routes | default([]) if route.vrf == mapping.vrf_name %}
  ip route {{ route.prefix }} {{ route.nexthop }}
{%- endfor %}
  address-family ipv4 unicast
{%- if vxlan.evpn.rt_format %}
    route-target both {{ vxlan.evpn.rt_format | replace('{vni}', mapping.l3_vni | string) }}
    route-target both {{ vxlan.evpn.rt_format | replace('{vni}', mapping.l3_vni | string) }} evpn
{%- endif %}
{%- for rt in mapping.import_route_targets | default([]) %}
    route-target import {{ rt }}
    route-target import {{ rt }} evpn
{%- endfor %}
!
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif -%}
